From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pear <pear@localhost>
Date: Mon, 17 Sep 2001 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [model] feat: Qwen3.5's vision tower sharded over the Ulysses
 sequence-parallel ranks

Under Ulysses sequence parallelism each rank encodes a share of the whole images and the ranks all-gather the
features; the backward all-reduces the gradients in fp32. Fewer images than ranks, extra forward arguments or an
unexpected token count take the stock forward.
